The class `ParallelFromArray` is a thin delegating wrapper that merely stores an array of `Publisher`s and forwards subscription calls after validation. It contains no computational logic, algorithmic complexity, or performance‑critical paths that would benefit from micro‑benchmarking. JMH benchmarks are intended for measuring the performance characteristics of non‑trivial code sections (e.g., loops, data structures, concurrency mechanisms). In this case, any benchmark would only capture framework overhead rather than meaningful application behavior, making a JMH test unnecessary.